1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:04,639
Shift's over. Who keeps the promise to call back?

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,368
Ha hands over three cases, with promises for 10:00 and 11:00.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:30,187
Ha tags Baton. Powered by Claude Code, it reads the conversation and drafts a structured handover ticket. Ledger records version one. Ledger runs on Node.js, without AI. The model proposes; code records.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,824
Claim accepted.

5
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:50,956
Dung has personally claimed the case. A name in a summary does not create ownership: each incoming owner must claim their own cases. Ha requests a review. Then the customer moves the callback from 10:00 to 09:30. Version one still shows ten.

6
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,454
Ha invites Checker into the Switch room. No briefing.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:22,550
Checker runs on Codex. Joining mid-handover, it reads the shared room history and standard operating procedure through Switch. No one repeats the brief. It spots the outdated 10:00 callback and two unclaimed cases, then asks Baton for version two. Switch gives a newly invited agent the context to contribute immediately.

8
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:42,072
Baton issues version two with 09:30. Ledger applies rule three: the promised time changed after Dung's earlier claim, so that claim needs renewal. Dung must explicitly accept the updated promise by claiming again.

9
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,509
Rule two rejects version one.

10
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:58,683
Dung personally claims all three cases on version two, then requests status. Only now does Ledger confirm: handover complete.

11
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:13,852
Dung asks what to tell the customer about SR-1077. Baton explains: NovaSoft's patch is still pending. Call at 09:30, and give an update without promising when the fix will arrive.

12
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:26,603
Eighteen scenarios passed 92 checks. Mutations caught. Ledger missed three risks outside its rules.

13
00:02:26,853 --> 00:02:36,621
Agent accuracy remains unmeasured. Models propose, code enforces, humans own the promise. Built on Switch.
